rutabaga_gfx: native contexts through the FFI, the fence ring index, polling, a logger, guest dma-bufs

The research's patches/rutabaga_gfx/changes.diff (git diff HEAD of its
checkout of 4fb9f32055d8, release 0.1.85, on 2026-10-12), unchanged
below this description:

- the FFI's virgl_renderer feature: DRM native contexts and virgl2
  through the C FFI that QEMU uses, beside cross-domain on one device,
  as crosvm's --features virgl_renderer;
- struct rutabaga_fence's ring_idx a uint8_t, as RutabagaFence's is in
  Rust: as a uint32_t a reader got three bytes of padding with it, the
  fences of rings other than 0 never matched their commands, and QEMU's
  control queue filled up (the display froze);
- rutabaga_poll_descriptor() and rutabaga_poll(): virglrenderer's DRM
  contexts retire their fences only from a poll;
- rutabaga's and virglrenderer's messages to stderr, which QEMU dropped
  (no logger): warnings and errors, RUTABAGA_LOG=off|error|warn|info|
  debug|trace for others, at most 50 at once then one a second;
- guest-memory blobs get the udmabuf of their pages QEMU makes
  (x-guest-dmabuf), through virglrenderer's
  virgl_renderer_resource_set_guest_dmabuf(), looked up at run time.

